Chapter: SpiderDeal

  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Games chapter Spider

 A fair draw agrees in parity about 100 times in 200; the draws that were
 one number's residues agreed 200 times. The second line reads about 14 on
 a fair two-suit deck and could not see that defect.

 We say:

Section: Probe

  parity-agree : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  parity-agree (seed) (last) (acc) =
    if seed > last then acc
    else let a = rng-mod (sp-draw seed 1) 2
    in let b = rng-mod (sp-draw seed 3) 2
    in parity-agree (seed + 1) last (acc + (if a == b then 1 else 0))

  deck-diff : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  deck-diff (seed) (last) (acc) =
    if seed > last then acc
    else let d = spider-deck-new seed 2
    in let top = list-at d 103
    in let under = list-at d 102
    in deck-diff (seed + 1) last (acc + (if sp-rank top == sp-rank under then 1 else 0))

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening =
    let a = parity-agree 1 200 0
    in let b = deck-diff 1 200 0
    in act
      print-line-uni ("draws at i=1 and i=3 agree in parity: " & show a & " of 200")
      print-line-uni ("top two cards of the deck share a rank: " & show b & " of 200")
    end

